    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# With Image Workflow\n\nThis n8n flow starts when a form with an image is submitted:\n1. The image is converted into Base64.\n2. Sent to Google’s **Gemini 2.5 Flash Image** (Nano-Banana) API via HTTP.\n3. The API returns the edited image, which is converted back into a usable file.\n\nWith the API, handling advanced image editing becomes simple—you just send a request and get back a ready result.\n\n---\n\n## Without Image Workflow\n\nThis lightweight version skips file handling. Trigger manually, send a text prompt directly to Nano-Banana API, and instantly receive the generated output.\n\nPerfect for quick prototyping and testing prompts.\n\n---\n\n### 🔗 Connect with Me\n\nWant to learn how to build controller-agent logic in n8n using LLMs and conditions?\n\n📺 **YouTube** → [@tech.mayankagg](https://www.youtube.com/@tech.mayankagg/)  \n💼 **LinkedIn** → [Mayank Agarwal](https://www.linkedin.com/in/mayank953/)  \n📸 **Instagram** → [@tech.mayankagg](https://www.instagram.com/tech.mayankagg/)\n\n---\n\n*Shared by Mayank Agarwal – Teaching AI workflows that actually scale.*\n",
        "height": 944,
        "width": 944,
        "color": 4
      },
